eads pin, README, schemas. If the real tree is dirty (modified emit_custody.py), the tool doesn't care about git. Fine. But `rc` must be 0 unless the emitter claim LIES. Since we keep the literal at 0.9.8 equal to the pin, rc=0.\n\nOK. Now the main work: implement resolution in `kit/emit_custody.py`.\n\n### Implementation plan for emit_custody.py\n\n1. Keep `SPEC_VERSION = \"0.9.8\"` with a comment explaining it is the emitter's declared baseline, retained for `tools/check_version_claims.py`; it is no longer stamped.\n\nHmm wait. Actually, there's a subtlety: if `SPEC_VERSION` is retained but unused, a linter would complain but that's fine.\n\nBut maybe better: keep it and use it as the *expected* default in a way that never stamps. E.g.:\n\n```python\nSPEC_VERSION = \"0.9.8\"   # the version this emitter was cut against; a record's specVersion is resolved (see resolve_spec_version)\n```\n\n2. Add a `resolve_spec_version(job, ci, override, ref) -> tuple[str|None, dict]` that:\n   - reads `ci.get(\"custody_spec\")` (a str path). Resolve relative to job dir.\n   - if doc present:\n     - check it exists, is a directory\n     - `SPEC.md` exists\n     - parse `**Version X.Y.Z ...**` from SPEC.md\n     - if a git repo at that dir answers `rev-parse HEAD`:\n       - find the containing work tree (git -C dir rev-parse --show-toplevel), get its HEAD\n       - require they match, else refuse\n     - if override given and differs from the document version \u2192 refuse naming the collision\n     - return version, {\"source\": \"document\", \"path\": <path of SPEC.md, job-relative or absolute?>, \"sha256\": ..., \"origin\": \"document\"}\n   - else if override given:\n     - validate it's X.Y.Z (well-formed). If malformed \u2192 refuse? probably.\n     - return version, {\"origin\": \"--spec-version\", \"source\": \"--spec-version\"?}\n   - else: refuse with kind \"spec-version\".\n\nWhat exactly does `version_block` require in case 1? `block.get(\"sha256\")` == sha of SPEC.md