t, gaps, ref, now, expect, allow_hand,\n                            ci=ci if isinstance(ci, dict) else None, override=spec_version)\n    ci = load(inputs_path) if have_inputs else None\n```\n\nAnd the signature of `build` gains `spec_version: str | None = None`.\n\nNow the inputs path: after `ci = load(...)`, resolution:\n\nWhere exactly? After `rev = H.revision(...)` and before `pred = {...}`. But `pred` is constructed far below. Let's call resolution right after `ev_log`/`lines` setup or right after `rev`. Simplest: right after `rev`:\n\n```python\n    version, version_block = resolve_spec_version(job, ci, spec_version, ref)\n```\n\nThen in the `pred` dict, replace `\"specVersion\": SPEC_VERSION,` with `\"specVersion\": version,`.\n\nAnd add `xp[\"spec_version\"] = version_block` somewhere before `pred[\"x-plumbline\"] = xp`. There's a block:\n\n```python\n    xp[\"schema\"] = \"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"\n    xp[\"hand_times\"] = [hand[k] for k in hand]\n```\n\nWe can insert after `xp[\"schema\"] = ...`:\n\n```python\n    if version_block:\n        xp[\"spec_version\"] = version_block\n```\n\nHmm, but if `version_block` is empty we omit the key. In case 3, block has origin \"--spec-version\" \u2192 non-empty. In case 1, block non-empty. Good.\n\nAlso, should the inputs path put `spec_version` unconditionally? If refusal, nothing is written. Fine.\n\nNow `build_finish`: replace `\"specVersion\": SPEC_VERSION,` with `\"specVersion\": version,` and add `xp[\"spec_version\"] = version_block` near `xp[\"schema\"] = ...`.\n\nNow `main()`: add the argument and pass it.\n\n```python\n    ap.add_argument(\"--spec-version\", help=\"the custody spec version the record attests, when the job names no \"\n                                           \"custody document (X.Y.Z); the record's origin says the flag\")\n```\nand\n\n```python\n        record, gaps, _ = build(job, inputs, ref, expect=a.expect_revision, allow_hand=a.allow_hand_times,\n                                spec